From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: link to bare_app

bare_app (the SDK's LVGL launcher for the ODROID-GO Advance) starts the
client as a game in its own process, with a socket and shared memory
(bare_app's src/games/game_ipc.h). With SDL's dummy video driver the
window, twice the size of bare_app's video layer, stays in memory: after
each SDL_RenderPresent its content goes to bare_app scaled down 2:1, or a
1:1 part around the cursor (L1 switches). Gamepad messages become SDL game
controller events, so VCMI's own controller support drives the game. The
D-pad moves the magnifier off the cursor (once the stick moves, the cursor
comes into view at the edge it was beyond), or in the overview scrolls
the adventure map wherever the cursor is; the map
scrolls at a screen border only while the stick pushes that way, since
the stick leaves the cursor there.

The link also sets what a handheld needs: quiet logging (the default
traces into a file on the SD card), no second stick dead zone. And it removes per-frame and per-step work that a Cortex-A35
cannot afford, found by profiling on the device:
- the screen texture has the window's format and is not cleared first,
  so presenting is a copy instead of a per-pixel blend plus a fill;
- while a hero walks, the info bar is rebuilt once per walk, not per
  tile, and changed tiles redraw only the minimap, not the whole
  adventure map (both ran under the interface lock and stopped the walk
  at every tile).

Languages, without VCMI's launcher:
- bare_app's language (BARE_APP_LANG) is set right after the settings
  load, before the mods: set later, the translation mods followed it only
  at the next start;
- a translation for another language than the selected one stays enabled
  (it is not loaded): VCMI turned it off for good, and only its launcher
  turns it back on;
- text that should be Western (CP1252) but is mostly Cyrillic letters of
  CP1251 is read as CP1251. Maps and campaigns do not say their encoding
  and VCMI reads them with the selected language's one, so a Russian
  edition's maps turned into garbage in English.

Built only with -DVCMI_BARE_APP_IPC=<bare_app's src directory>; the
client finds out at run time whether bare_app started it, and behaves
as upstream otherwise.

Upstream: not applicable (SDK-specific)
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
